		Paragraph: Once upon a time, in a valley among beech forests, a village filled its square with chestnuts every autumn. The smoke of the roasters rose above the roofs and the whole valley smelled of it for a week, while the children ran between the stalls and the old people counted the sacks that came down from the hills on the backs of the mules.
